<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111155" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλόζω-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fond of one's life,</i> with collat. sense of
				<i>cowardly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βροτοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					816.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				19
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Charito
				3.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. οἱ πρεσβύτεροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1389b32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mort.</u>
					39
				</span></i>
			
			 (misspelt <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ζωιον,</span> s.
			v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ind.Sto.</u>
				27
			</span></i>: as Subst., <i>coward,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.269
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> of patients
			in disease, <i>desirous of living,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of plants,
				<i>tenacious of life,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				7.13.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>evergreen,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Al.</u>
				274
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				591
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλόζῳος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷον</span>)
				<i>fond of animals,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημιουργός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					1.4.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.305
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>delighting to produce life,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cleom.
					1.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
